\title{Additive group, additive set, sumset}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2023-10-01}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{We shall consider additively written Abelian groups: we call them \em{additive groups}. Also, an \em{additive set} is a finite nonempty subset of an additive group.}

\p{Given additive sets #{A, B}, their sum (also called ‘Minkowski sum’) is}

##{A + B = \lbrace a + b : a \in A, b \in B\rbrace .}
